  "critique": {
    "axis": "aesthetics",
    "evidence": "Strong cyber-defense art direction: disciplined cyan/coral palette, crisp borders, expressive risk visualization, and clear desktop control/results hierarchy. However, tablet becomes excessively tall and visually monotonous, while mobile typography is often too small and tightly set, weakening readability and polish. The mobile header drops the brand name and exposes only a cramped partial navigation rail; tablet navigation is similarly clipped. The desktop header also shows oversized ghost lettering behind the navigation, creating distracting visual noise.",
    "fix": "Increase mobile supporting-text and label sizes, loosen dense result copy, and reduce tablet vertical padding. Replace the clipped header rail with a deliberate compact navigation pattern that preserves branding and current-section context. Remove or substantially soften the desktop header’s ghost lettering.",
